SWEET AUDIO (patch 0378, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A9), boot-arg sweetaoc=4 together with sweetamp=1. Runs the A8 start of patch 0377 unchanged;
after "online" (sweet_aoc_start.c swau_run): maps the IPC window again and calls the amp run of patch 0373 (sweet_amp.c sweet_amp_audio_run, late, with
the touch thread up: gpp23 DAT race documented there) with two callbacks. Inside it, between the init of both amps and the restore (sweet_amp.h
amp_a9_part): A9b the TDM0 config of stock cs35l41 set_pdata / set_dai_fmt / set_sysclk / hw_params (23 cited rows, each a (register, mask, field)
merge allowed only while armed against the word just read; PWR_CTRL1 0x2014 / GLOBAL_EN read only, refused by name, never written), then A9a the AOC
open (sweet_audio.h: audio_output_control queue I/O as aoc_ipc_core.c, doorbell AOC mailbox INTGR0, commands GET_DSP_STATE 233 and BIND2 271
src 0 -> SINK_SPEAKER bind 1), the PLL lock read (IRQ1_STATUS3 PLL_LOCK, <= 100 x 1 ms per amp), the AOC close (BIND2 bind 0 whenever a bind 1 may
have been sent), then the 0373 restore (both resets low, every word back). A9c: sweet_cs_dsp.h parses the HALO .wmfw / .bin as Linux v6.18 cs_dsp
(host test on the stock files); NOT loaded, nothing included by the kernel. Pass line "SWEET AUDIO: tdm0 up, amp pll locked l,r, dsp not loaded".
Also: the A8 line "ssmt ... restored 1" now reads "written-back 0 kept 1" (the bypass was never written back once the AOC started).
Host tests: shim/aoc_audio_host_test.c (fake AOC queue peer + parser), shim/amp_xnu_host_test.c (+ A9 register / PLL model). BUILT, UNRUN.

